Name what ffsubsync actually does, and show LOADING while languages are read

Three situations shared one progress label. With a sibling-subtitle reference (the usual path for
embedded tracks in a file with several text tracks) the phase kept the placeholder "Analyzing
speech" that was set before the branch was decided, so an 0.6 s subtitle comparison looked like a
fresh audio analysis on every subtitle of the same file - reported as "it analyses the same
episode each sub when it is supposed to use cache".

The label now comes from one testable helper: "Syncing (from cache)" when the stored analysis is
reused, "Syncing (analysing the audio)" when the audio is analysed, and "Syncing (using another
subtitle track)" when a sibling track is the reference and no audio work happens. Checks assert
that no label claims speech analysis when none occurs.

The language dropdown showed "All languages" while it was still querying subtitle lists, claiming
completeness it did not have. It now shows LOADING with the real count and is disabled until the
list is in.

Version 1.1.0.33.
